{"sections":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Fixed return values only go so far. Real dependencies ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"compute","type":"text"}]},{"text":": a calculator multiplies its operands, a sync engine mutates state, a network service delivers results through callbacks.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In this tutorial you’ll stub with closures that receive the actual arguments — fully typed, no casting — learn how overlapping stubs resolve, register side effects, and drive callback-based APIs on your terms.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"backgroundImage":"intro-dynamic.png","chapter":"Advanced Stubbing and Verification","kind":"hero","image":"intro-dynamic.png","title":"Stub Dynamically","estimatedTimeInMinutes":10},{"tasks":[{"stepsSection":[{"runtimePreview":null,"type":"step","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Create a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Calculator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" protocol and mark it mockable:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"code":"03-1-1-calculator.swift","media":null,"caption":[]},{"code":"03-1-2-computed.swift","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Stub multiplication with a closure. Note that "},{"code":"a","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"b","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" are plain "},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s — there is no casting, ever:"}]}],"media":null,"runtimePreview":null,"caption":[],"type":"step"}],"anchor":"Return-computed-values","contentSection":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Instead of handing ","type":"text"},{"code":"thenReturn","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" a value, hand it a closure. The closure’s parameters are the mocked method’s parameters — concrete types guaranteed by parameter packs. You are, in effect, substituting the method’s implementation.","type":"text"}]}],"mediaPosition":"trailing","media":"intro-dynamic.png","kind":"contentAndMedia"}],"title":"Return computed values"},{"stepsSection":[{"code":"03-2-1-ordering.swift","runtimePreview":null,"caption":[],"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Register specific matchers first and the broad fallback last, then exercise the boundaries:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"step","media":null}],"contentSection":[{"mediaPosition":"trailing","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Stubs with different matchers coexist: the most specific matcher that matches a call answers it. When you register another stub for the "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"same","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" matcher, the later registration wins."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"contentAndMedia","media":"chapter-advanced.png"}],"title":"Order your stubs","anchor":"Order-your-stubs"},{"stepsSection":[{"type":"step","caption":[],"code":"03-3-1-sync-engine.swift","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Declare a ","type":"text"},{"code":"SyncEngine","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" dependency whose refresh method returns ","type":"text"},{"code":"Void","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"runtimePreview":null,"media":null},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Register an action with "},{"code":".do","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", then pair it with a "},{"code":"thenReturn(())","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" stub for the same matcher so the call itself resolves cleanly. Every refresh appends to the array:"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"step","runtimePreview":null,"caption":[],"media":null,"code":"03-3-2-side-effects.swift"}],"contentSection":[{"kind":"contentAndMedia","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Sometimes you want to observe or record without changing the response. ","type":"text"},{"code":".do","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" registers an action alongside the stub — it runs with the call’s arguments whenever a matching invocation occurs.","type":"text"}]}],"mediaPosition":"trailing","media":"intro-dynamic.png"}],"title":"Run side effects with do","anchor":"Run-side-effects-with-do"},{"title":"Drive callback-based APIs","contentSection":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Completion-handler APIs are where mocks earn their keep. Match the closure parameter with ","type":"text"},{"code":".any","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the only matcher that makes sense for it — then invoke the completion yourself from a ","type":"text"},{"code":"thenReturn","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" closure. You decide when and with what the callback fires.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"media":"chapter-advanced.png","mediaPosition":"trailing","kind":"contentAndMedia"}],"stepsSection":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NetworkService"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol with a completion handler, plus a small "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"User"},{"type":"text","text":" model:"}]}],"type":"step","media":null,"code":"03-4-1-network-service.swift","runtimePreview":null,"caption":[]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Stub the call, invoke the completion with a success result, and assert what arrives. The closure’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" parameter is the real ","type":"text"},{"code":"String","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that was passed in:","type":"text"}]}],"type":"step","media":null,"code":"03-4-2-callbacks.swift","runtimePreview":null,"caption":[]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Failures are one line away — deliver "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".failure(...)"},{"type":"text","text":" instead and your error paths become just as testable as the happy path."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"step","media":null,"code":null,"runtimePreview":null,"caption":[]}],"anchor":"Drive-callback-based-APIs"}],"kind":"tasks"},{"kind":"assessments","assessments":[{"title":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Inside "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"when(mock.calculate(a: .any, b: .any)).thenReturn { a, b in ... }"},{"type":"text","text":", what are "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"a"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"b"},{"type":"text","text":"?"}]}],"content":[],"choices":[{"isCorrect":false,"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Any"},{"type":"text","text":" values you must cast to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"justification":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Parameter packs preserve the method’s concrete parameter types — that’s the headline feature."}]}]},{"isCorrect":true,"justification":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The closure type is derived from the mocked method’s parameters, so the compiler enforces it."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Real ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s, statically typed to match the method’s signature."}]}]},{"justification":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Matchers select which calls match; the closure receives the already-extracted arguments.","type":"text"}]}],"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ArgMatcher<Int>"},{"type":"text","text":" values you unwrap manually."}]}],"isCorrect":false}],"type":"multiple-choice"},{"type":"multiple-choice","title":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You stub "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".any"},{"text":" first, then stub the exact value ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"42"},{"type":"text","text":" for the same method. A call with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"42"},{"type":"text","text":" returns…"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"content":[],"choices":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Whatever "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".any"},{"type":"text","text":" returns — stubs can’t overlap."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"isCorrect":false,"justification":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Stubs absolutely overlap; matching is what decides."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"42","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" stub’s value — the more specific matcher wins."}]}],"isCorrect":true,"justification":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The most specific matching stub answers the call; "},{"code":".any","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" remains the fallback."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The most recently registered stub, always."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"justification":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Recency only decides between stubs for the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"same"}]},{"type":"text","text":" matcher, not across different matchers."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"isCorrect":false}]}],"anchor":"Check-Your-Understanding"},{"kind":"callToAction","action":{"overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Get started"}],"overridingTitle":"Get started","isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/verifying-interactions"},"abstract":[{"text":"You’ve verified counts and matched arguments. This page completes the toolkit: asserting a call happened ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"never","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", proving a mock was ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"untouched"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", and — the signature feature — verifying the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"order","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" of calls as they happened across multiple mocks."}],"title":"Verify Every Interaction","featuredEyebrow":"Tutorial"}],"kind":"project","variants":[{"paths":["\/tutorials\/swiftmocking\/dynamic-stubbing"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/dynamic-stubbing"},"hierarchy":{"modules":[{"projects":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/mocking-your-first-protocol","sections":[{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/mocking-your-first-protocol#Mark-a-protocol-as-mockable"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/mocking-your-first-protocol#Create-the-system-under-test"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/mocking-your-first-protocol#Stub-return-values-with-when"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/mocking-your-first-protocol#Verify-the-interaction"},{"kind":"assessment","reference":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/mocking-your-first-protocol#Check-Your-Understanding"}]}],"reference":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents\/Getting-Started"},{"projects":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/matching-arguments","sections":[{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/matching-arguments#Match-any-or-exactly-one"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/matching-arguments#Match-with-predicates-and-ranges"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/matching-arguments#Capture-and-inspect-arguments"},{"kind":"assessment","reference":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/matching-arguments#Check-Your-Understanding"}]}],"reference":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents\/Argument-Matching"},{"projects":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/dynamic-stubbing","sections":[{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/dynamic-stubbing#Return-computed-values"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/dynamic-stubbing#Order-your-stubs"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/dynamic-stubbing#Run-side-effects-with-do"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/dynamic-stubbing#Drive-callback-based-APIs"},{"kind":"assessment","reference":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/dynamic-stubbing#Check-Your-Understanding"}]},{"reference":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/verifying-interactions","sections":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/verifying-interactions#Assert-call-counts","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/verifying-interactions#Verify-order-across-mocks","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/verifying-interactions#Debug-failing-verifications","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/verifying-interactions#Check-Your-Understanding","kind":"assessment"}]}],"reference":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents\/Advanced-Stubbing-and-Verification"}],"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents","doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents\/$volume","doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents\/Advanced-Stubbing-and-Verification"]],"reference":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents"},"metadata":{"category":"SwiftMocking","categoryPathComponent":"Table-Of-Contents","role":"project","title":"Stub Dynamically"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"references":{"doc://SwiftMocking/tutorials/Table-Of-Contents/Getting-Started":{"url":"\/tutorials\/table-of-contents\/getting-started","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents\/Getting-Started","type":"topic","title":"Getting Started","role":"article","abstract":[]},"intro-dynamic.png":{"type":"image","variants":[{"url":"\/images\/SwiftMocking\/intro-dynamic.png","traits":["1x","light"]}],"identifier":"intro-dynamic.png","alt":"A mock method call branching into a spy notebook recording its arguments."},"doc://SwiftMocking/tutorials/SwiftMocking/verifying-interactions#Verify-order-across-mocks":{"role":"pseudoSymbol","url":"\/tutorials\/swiftmocking\/verifying-interactions#Verify-order-across-mocks","abstract":[{"text":"You’ve verified counts and matched arguments. This page completes the toolkit: asserting a call happened ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"never"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", proving a mock was ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"untouched","type":"text"}]},{"text":", and — the signature feature — verifying the ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"order","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" of calls as they happened across multiple mocks."}],"title":"Verify order across mocks","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/verifying-interactions#Verify-order-across-mocks","type":"section","kind":"section"},"doc://SwiftMocking/tutorials/SwiftMocking/dynamic-stubbing#Order-your-stubs":{"title":"Order your stubs","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed return values only go so far. Real dependencies "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"compute","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":": a calculator multiplies its operands, a sync engine mutates state, a network service delivers results through callbacks."}],"role":"pseudoSymbol","kind":"section","type":"section","url":"\/tutorials\/swiftmocking\/dynamic-stubbing#Order-your-stubs","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/dynamic-stubbing#Order-your-stubs"},"doc://SwiftMocking/tutorials/SwiftMocking/dynamic-stubbing#Check-Your-Understanding":{"url":"\/tutorials\/swiftmocking\/dynamic-stubbing#Check-Your-Understanding","type":"link","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/dynamic-stubbing#Check-Your-Understanding","title":"Check Your Understanding","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Check Your Understanding"}]},"doc://SwiftMocking/tutorials/SwiftMocking/verifying-interactions#Debug-failing-verifications":{"title":"Debug failing verifications","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"You’ve verified counts and matched arguments. This page completes the toolkit: asserting a call happened "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"never"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":", proving a mock was "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"untouched"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":", and — the signature feature — verifying the "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"order"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" of calls as they happened across multiple mocks."}],"role":"pseudoSymbol","kind":"section","type":"section","url":"\/tutorials\/swiftmocking\/verifying-interactions#Debug-failing-verifications","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/verifying-interactions#Debug-failing-verifications"},"doc://SwiftMocking/tutorials/SwiftMocking/mocking-your-first-protocol#Stub-return-values-with-when":{"url":"\/tutorials\/swiftmocking\/mocking-your-first-protocol#Stub-return-values-with-when","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/mocking-your-first-protocol#Stub-return-values-with-when","role":"pseudoSymbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"In this tutorial you’ll test a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":" that depends on a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PricingService"},{"type":"text","text":" — without writing a mock class by hand. You’ll mark a protocol with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Mockable"},{"type":"text","text":", let the macro generate the mock, stub what its method returns, and verify that your code actually called it."}],"title":"Stub return values with when","kind":"section","type":"section"},"03-3-2-side-effects.swift":{"highlights":[],"content":["func testSideEffects() {","    let mock = MockSyncEngine()","    var refreshed: [String] = []","","    \/\/ Observe every call with .do...","    when(mock.refresh(id: .any)).do { id in","        refreshed.append(id)","    }","    \/\/ ...and stub the same matcher so the call resolves cleanly.","    when(mock.refresh(id: .any)).thenReturn(())","","    mock.refresh(id: \"primary\")","    mock.refresh(id: \"backup\")","","    XCTAssertEqual(refreshed, [\"primary\", \"backup\"])","    verify(mock.refresh(id: .any)).called(2)","}"],"fileType":"swift","syntax":"swift","identifier":"03-3-2-side-effects.swift","type":"file","fileName":"SyncEngineTests.swift"},"doc://SwiftMocking/tutorials/Table-Of-Contents/Argument-Matching":{"role":"article","url":"\/tutorials\/table-of-contents\/argument-matching","abstract":[],"title":"Argument Matching","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents\/Argument-Matching","type":"topic","kind":"article"},"doc://SwiftMocking/tutorials/SwiftMocking/mocking-your-first-protocol#Verify-the-interaction":{"type":"section","kind":"section","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/mocking-your-first-protocol#Verify-the-interaction","title":"Verify the interaction","url":"\/tutorials\/swiftmocking\/mocking-your-first-protocol#Verify-the-interaction","abstract":[{"text":"In this tutorial you’ll test a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that depends on a ","type":"text"},{"code":"PricingService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — without writing a mock class by hand. You’ll mark a protocol with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Mockable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", let the macro generate the mock, stub what its method returns, and verify that your code actually called it.","type":"text"}],"role":"pseudoSymbol"},"doc://SwiftMocking/tutorials/SwiftMocking/matching-arguments#Match-any-or-exactly-one":{"url":"\/tutorials\/swiftmocking\/matching-arguments#Match-any-or-exactly-one","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/matching-arguments#Match-any-or-exactly-one","role":"pseudoSymbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Stubbing "},{"code":"\"apple\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and verifying "},{"code":".any","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is just the beginning. Real tests need finer control: "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"any","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" amount, amounts "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"under"}]},{"type":"text","text":" 100, codes "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"in"}]},{"type":"text","text":" a range, collections "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"of a certain size"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — or some predicate only you can express."}],"title":"Match any — or exactly one","kind":"section","type":"section"},"doc://SwiftMocking/tutorials/SwiftMocking/matching-arguments":{"url":"\/tutorials\/swiftmocking\/matching-arguments","estimatedTime":"10min","kind":"project","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/matching-arguments","type":"topic","title":"Match Arguments Precisely","role":"project","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Stubbing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"apple\""},{"type":"text","text":" and verifying "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".any"},{"type":"text","text":" is just the beginning. Real tests need finer control: "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"any"}]},{"text":" amount, amounts ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"under"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" 100, codes "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"in","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" a range, collections ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"of a certain size"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — or some predicate only you can express."}]},"doc://SwiftMocking/tutorials/Table-Of-Contents/Advanced-Stubbing-and-Verification":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents\/Advanced-Stubbing-and-Verification","title":"Advanced Stubbing and Verification","url":"\/tutorials\/table-of-contents\/advanced-stubbing-and-verification","abstract":[],"role":"article"},"doc://SwiftMocking/tutorials/SwiftMocking/mocking-your-first-protocol#Mark-a-protocol-as-mockable":{"title":"Mark a protocol as mockable","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"In this tutorial you’ll test a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":" that depends on a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PricingService"},{"type":"text","text":" — without writing a mock class by hand. You’ll mark a protocol with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Mockable"},{"type":"text","text":", let the macro generate the mock, stub what its method returns, and verify that your code actually called it."}],"role":"pseudoSymbol","kind":"section","type":"section","url":"\/tutorials\/swiftmocking\/mocking-your-first-protocol#Mark-a-protocol-as-mockable","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/mocking-your-first-protocol#Mark-a-protocol-as-mockable"},"doc://SwiftMocking/tutorials/SwiftMocking/matching-arguments#Capture-and-inspect-arguments":{"url":"\/tutorials\/swiftmocking\/matching-arguments#Capture-and-inspect-arguments","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/matching-arguments#Capture-and-inspect-arguments","kind":"section","type":"section","title":"Capture and inspect arguments","role":"pseudoSymbol","abstract":[{"text":"Stubbing ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"apple\""},{"type":"text","text":" and verifying "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".any"},{"type":"text","text":" is just the beginning. Real tests need finer control: "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"any","type":"text"}]},{"text":" amount, amounts ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"under","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" 100, codes ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"in","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" a range, collections "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"of a certain size","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" — or some predicate only you can express."}]},"doc://SwiftMocking/tutorials/SwiftMocking/dynamic-stubbing#Drive-callback-based-APIs":{"type":"section","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/dynamic-stubbing#Drive-callback-based-APIs","role":"pseudoSymbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed return values only go so far. Real dependencies "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"compute","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":": a calculator multiplies its operands, a sync engine mutates state, a network service delivers results through callbacks."}],"title":"Drive callback-based APIs","kind":"section","url":"\/tutorials\/swiftmocking\/dynamic-stubbing#Drive-callback-based-APIs"},"03-4-1-network-service.swift":{"highlights":[],"type":"file","fileType":"swift","identifier":"03-4-1-network-service.swift","syntax":"swift","content":["import SwiftMocking","","struct User: Equatable {","    let id: String","    let name: String","}","","@Mockable","protocol NetworkService {","    func fetchUser(id: String, completion: @escaping (Result<User, Error>) -> Void)","}"],"fileName":"NetworkService.swift"},"03-2-1-ordering.swift":{"identifier":"03-2-1-ordering.swift","fileType":"swift","fileName":"CalculatorTests.swift","syntax":"swift","highlights":[],"content":["func testStubOrdering() {","    let mock = MockCalculator()","","    let odd = ArgMatcher<Int>.any(that: { $0 % 2 == 1 })","","    \/\/ Specific matchers first...","    when(mock.calculate(a: odd, b: odd)).thenReturn { a, b in a * b }","    \/\/ ...broadest fallback last.","    when(mock.calculate(a: .any, b: .any)).thenReturn { a, b in a + b }","","    XCTAssertEqual(mock.calculate(a: 3, b: 3), 9, \"both odd — multiplied\")","    XCTAssertEqual(mock.calculate(a: 3, b: 4), 7, \"mixed — added\")","}"],"type":"file"},"doc://SwiftMocking/tutorials/SwiftMocking/verifying-interactions#Check-Your-Understanding":{"type":"link","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/verifying-interactions#Check-Your-Understanding","title":"Check Your Understanding","url":"\/tutorials\/swiftmocking\/verifying-interactions#Check-Your-Understanding","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Check Your Understanding"}]},"doc://SwiftMocking/tutorials/SwiftMocking/mocking-your-first-protocol":{"url":"\/tutorials\/swiftmocking\/mocking-your-first-protocol","estimatedTime":"10min","kind":"project","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/mocking-your-first-protocol","type":"topic","title":"Mock Your First Protocol","role":"project","abstract":[{"text":"In this tutorial you’ll test a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that depends on a ","type":"text"},{"code":"PricingService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — without writing a mock class by hand. You’ll mark a protocol with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Mockable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", let the macro generate the mock, stub what its method returns, and verify that your code actually called it.","type":"text"}]},"doc://SwiftMocking/tutorials/SwiftMocking/mocking-your-first-protocol#Check-Your-Understanding":{"titleInlineContent":[{"text":"Check Your Understanding","type":"text"}],"type":"link","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/mocking-your-first-protocol#Check-Your-Understanding","url":"\/tutorials\/swiftmocking\/mocking-your-first-protocol#Check-Your-Understanding","title":"Check Your Understanding"},"doc://SwiftMocking/tutorials/SwiftMocking/verifying-interactions#Assert-call-counts":{"url":"\/tutorials\/swiftmocking\/verifying-interactions#Assert-call-counts","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/verifying-interactions#Assert-call-counts","kind":"section","type":"section","title":"Assert call counts","role":"pseudoSymbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"You’ve verified counts and matched arguments. This page completes the toolkit: asserting a call happened "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"never"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", proving a mock was ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"untouched"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", and — the signature feature — verifying the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"order","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" of calls as they happened across multiple mocks.","type":"text"}]},"doc://SwiftMocking/tutorials/SwiftMocking/matching-arguments#Check-Your-Understanding":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/matching-arguments#Check-Your-Understanding","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"Check Your Understanding","type":"text"}],"url":"\/tutorials\/swiftmocking\/matching-arguments#Check-Your-Understanding","type":"link","title":"Check Your Understanding"},"03-3-1-sync-engine.swift":{"identifier":"03-3-1-sync-engine.swift","fileType":"swift","fileName":"SyncEngine.swift","syntax":"swift","highlights":[],"content":["import SwiftMocking","","@Mockable","protocol SyncEngine {","    func refresh(id: String) -> Void","}"],"type":"file"},"doc://SwiftMocking/tutorials/SwiftMocking/dynamic-stubbing":{"title":"Stub Dynamically","estimatedTime":"10min","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed return values only go so far. Real dependencies "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"compute","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": a calculator multiplies its operands, a sync engine mutates state, a network service delivers results through callbacks."}],"role":"project","kind":"project","type":"topic","url":"\/tutorials\/swiftmocking\/dynamic-stubbing","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/dynamic-stubbing"},"doc://SwiftMocking/tutorials/SwiftMocking/matching-arguments#Match-with-predicates-and-ranges":{"role":"pseudoSymbol","url":"\/tutorials\/swiftmocking\/matching-arguments#Match-with-predicates-and-ranges","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Stubbing "},{"code":"\"apple\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and verifying "},{"code":".any","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is just the beginning. Real tests need finer control: "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"any","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" amount, amounts "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"under","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" 100, codes "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"in"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" a range, collections "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"of a certain size","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" — or some predicate only you can express."}],"title":"Match with predicates and ranges","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/matching-arguments#Match-with-predicates-and-ranges","type":"section","kind":"section"},"chapter-advanced.png":{"variants":[{"traits":["1x","light"],"url":"\/images\/SwiftMocking\/chapter-advanced.png"}],"type":"image","alt":"A mock network service handing a result to a completion callback held by a test.","identifier":"chapter-advanced.png"},"doc://SwiftMocking/tutorials/SwiftMocking/verifying-interactions":{"url":"\/tutorials\/swiftmocking\/verifying-interactions","role":"project","estimatedTime":"10min","kind":"project","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"You’ve verified counts and matched arguments. This page completes the toolkit: asserting a call happened ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"never"}]},{"type":"text","text":", proving a mock was "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"untouched"}]},{"type":"text","text":", and — the signature feature — verifying the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"order","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" of calls as they happened across multiple mocks."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/verifying-interactions","title":"Verify Every Interaction"},"doc://SwiftMocking/tutorials/SwiftMocking/dynamic-stubbing#Run-side-effects-with-do":{"url":"\/tutorials\/swiftmocking\/dynamic-stubbing#Run-side-effects-with-do","kind":"section","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/dynamic-stubbing#Run-side-effects-with-do","type":"section","title":"Run side effects with do","role":"pseudoSymbol","abstract":[{"text":"Fixed return values only go so far. Real dependencies ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"compute","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":": a calculator multiplies its operands, a sync engine mutates state, a network service delivers results through callbacks."}]},"03-1-1-calculator.swift":{"highlights":[],"content":["import SwiftMocking","","@Mockable","protocol Calculator {","    func calculate(a: Int, b: Int) -> Int","}"],"fileType":"swift","syntax":"swift","identifier":"03-1-1-calculator.swift","type":"file","fileName":"Calculator.swift"},"03-1-2-computed.swift":{"highlights":[],"content":["func testComputedReturn() {","    let mock = MockCalculator()","","    \/\/ a and b are real Ints — no casting, ever.","    when(mock.calculate(a: .any, b: .any)).thenReturn { a, b in","        a * b","    }","","    XCTAssertEqual(mock.calculate(a: 6, b: 7), 42)","}"],"fileType":"swift","syntax":"swift","identifier":"03-1-2-computed.swift","type":"file","fileName":"CalculatorTests.swift"},"doc://SwiftMocking/tutorials/SwiftMocking/mocking-your-first-protocol#Create-the-system-under-test":{"title":"Create the system under test","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"In this tutorial you’ll test a "},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that depends on a "},{"code":"PricingService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — without writing a mock class by hand. You’ll mark a protocol with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Mockable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", let the macro generate the mock, stub what its method returns, and verify that your code actually called it."}],"role":"pseudoSymbol","kind":"section","type":"section","url":"\/tutorials\/swiftmocking\/mocking-your-first-protocol#Create-the-system-under-test","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/mocking-your-first-protocol#Create-the-system-under-test"},"doc://SwiftMocking/tutorials/Table-Of-Contents":{"url":"\/tutorials\/table-of-contents","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents","kind":"overview","type":"topic","title":"Meet SwiftMocking","role":"overview","abstract":[{"text":"Stop hand-writing mock classes. With SwiftMocking, one ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Mockable"},{"text":" annotation turns any protocol into a fully featured mock: stub return values, match arguments with expressive matchers, drive callbacks, and verify every interaction — all type-safe, all local, no code generation steps in your build.","type":"text"}]},"doc://SwiftMocking/tutorials/SwiftMocking/dynamic-stubbing#Return-computed-values":{"url":"\/tutorials\/swiftmocking\/dynamic-stubbing#Return-computed-values","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/dynamic-stubbing#Return-computed-values","role":"pseudoSymbol","abstract":[{"text":"Fixed return values only go so far. Real dependencies ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"compute","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":": a calculator multiplies its operands, a sync engine mutates state, a network service delivers results through callbacks.","type":"text"}],"title":"Return computed values","kind":"section","type":"section"},"03-4-2-callbacks.swift":{"highlights":[],"content":["func testFetchUserDeliversSuccess() {","    let mock = MockNetworkService()","    let received = expectation(description: \"completion invoked\")","","    \/\/ .any is the only matcher that makes sense for a closure parameter.","    when(mock.fetchUser(id: .equal(\"42\"), completion: .any)).thenReturn { id, completion in","        completion(.success(User(id: id, name: \"Test User\")))","    }","","    mock.fetchUser(id: \"42\") { result in","        XCTAssertEqual(try result.get(), User(id: \"42\", name: \"Test User\"))","        received.fulfill()","    }","","    wait(for: [received], timeout: 1.0)","}"],"fileType":"swift","syntax":"swift","identifier":"03-4-2-callbacks.swift","type":"file","fileName":"NetworkServiceTests.swift"}}}